# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Windows
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# LEGO SPIKE app scratch files — keep exported .llsp3 in code/spike-projects/
*.llsp3.bak
~$*

# Large media: put raw video in shared cloud storage, link to it instead.
# Committing 4K match footage will make this repo painful to clone.
*.mov
*.mp4
*.avi

# Presentation exports that can be regenerated
*.pptx.tmp

# FIRST's season materials.
#
# Per team decision (9 Aug 2026), these ARE committed so everyone gets them
# with a clone instead of re-downloading. Two caveats worth remembering:
#
#   1. This repo is PUBLIC, so these become publicly visible. They're FIRST's
#      copyrighted material — fine for a team repo, but a deliberate choice.
#      If that ever becomes a problem, going private also kills the free
#      GitHub Pages site.
#   2. Committed binaries live in git history forever. Removing them later
#      needs a history rewrite, not just a delete.
#
# The missions video stays out: at 1.3GB it exceeds GitHub's 100MB hard
# per-file limit and the push would be rejected. Stream it from the FIRST
# Season Resources page instead.
docs/official-materials/*.mp4
docs/official-materials/*.mov

# Junk from the download — HTML pages saved without an extension
docs/official-materials/scoresheet
docs/official-materials/wDan0826cn0

# MkDocs build output — the site is built by CI, not committed
site/
.cache/

# Python virtualenv, if you preview the site locally
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
